Aardvark Joe wrote:

> One thing that isn't really finalized is the "notable achievements"
> section. [...]
> Comments on other events that might be tracked are welcome.

I would find it interesting if it would also keep track of:

- Picking up artifacts for the first time (kind, turn number, maybe also 
dtype + dlvl)
- Picking up amulets of life saving and wands of wishing (turn number, 
maybe also dtype + dlvl) (are there other important items that are 
relatively rare and considered useful?)
- Getting a wish (wished for object, what the player got if differing, 
turn number and source (fountain / magic lamp / wand of wishing))
- Genociding something (genocided monster type(s), turn number and 
source (scroll / throne))
- Entering the Quest / Medusa / Sokoban / the last level of Sokoban / 
the nines / mine town / the bottom of the mines and so on (the turn 
number is important here)
- Breaking a conduct (type and turn number)
- Killing an unique monster for the first time (name and turn number)

Note that all these would need more than a simple bit mask because they 
have additional information associated with them. I think they would 
also work better when the format of the log entry would be changed slightly.

I'm pretty sure I'm forgetting other important events in NetHack games 
so feel free to add them.

